# =====================================================================
# mikrotik_admin_rotate_delta — HD-321: rotate shared RouterOS admin password
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------
# Vault `mikrotik-admin_login` is the SSOT: `old-password` = the value being
# superseded (now FAILING), `password` = the new live value (the only one the
# converge/initial templates render, via the render playbook's 1Password
# lookup). This minimal delta applies ONLY the admin password change to a
# device — lighter than re-applying a full converge, sanctioned by
# network-ops.md §Rotating the shared admin password (HD-321).
#
# Apply per device (RB4011 10.10.99.1, CRS328 10.10.99.2, APs .4/.5/.6):
#   bash scripts/routeros-apply-delta.sh <device> mikrotik_admin_rotate_delta.rsc
# The drop-in goes through the SSH `ansible` identity (key-only — unaffected by
# the admin password rotation) + pinned host key, never prints key material.
# Re-render before every rotation so the .rsc embeds the CURRENT vault value.
# Render: playbooks/render-converge.yml; verify per device from a Mgmt-sourced
# API path (old-password must FAIL, password must authenticate).
# =====================================================================
/user set [find name=admin] password="{{ mikrotik_admin_password }}" comment="human admin (rotated HD-321)"
# =====================================================================
# Verify (from the management plane, NOT a non-Mgmt source which the input
# filter drops and could read as a false lockout):
#   old-password from the vault  -> API login FAIL
#   password from the vault      -> API login OK
# =====================================================================